<!-- ================= FEATURES ================= -->
<section class="sec" id="features">
  <div class="wrap">
    <header class="sec-head rv">
      <div class="sh-top"><span class="sec-no">(02)</span><span>FEATURES</span><span class="sh-rule"></span></div>
      <h2>More than a <em class="grad">gallery.</em></h2>
      <p class="sec-sub">The feed, reels and discovery you already know, rebuilt around your own photos and videos. No cloud library required.</p>
    </header>
    <div class="feats" id="feats">
      <div class="feat open rv">
        <button class="feat-head" id="fh1" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="fb1">
          <span class="f-no">01</span><span class="f-title">The home feed</span><span class="f-tag">DOOMSCROLL</span>
          <span class="f-chev"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"/></svg></span>
        </button>
        <div class="feat-body" id="fb1" role="region" aria-labelledby="fh1"><div class="fb-in"><div>
          <p>An endless vertical feed of your own archive, mixed across every folder. <strong>Recent</strong> for the new stuff, <strong>Rediscover</strong> to resurface old shots you forgot you took, <strong>Random</strong> when you want the algorithm to be a die roll instead.</p>
          <p class="f-mono2">Recent · Rediscover · Random. One tap apart.</p>
        </div></div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="feat rv" style="--d:.05s">
        <button class="feat-head" id="fh2" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="fb2">
          <span class="f-no">02</span><span class="f-title">Stories &amp; highlights</span><span class="f-tag">TAP-THROUGH</span>
          <span class="f-chev"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"/></svg></span>
        </button>
        <div class="feat-body" id="fb2" role="region" aria-labelledby="fh2"><div class="fb-in"><div>
          <p>Add photos or videos to <code>AppFolder/stories/</code> for an avatar story, and use its child folders for named highlights. The Home rail separately shows date-based <strong>Moments</strong>, or <strong>Highlights</strong> when capture dates are sparse. Story viewing is full-screen and tap-through.</p>
          <p class="f-mono2">AppFolder/stories/ · AppFolder/stories/Trip/</p>
        </div></div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="feat rv" style="--d:.1s">
        <button class="feat-head" id="fh3" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="fb3">
          <span class="f-no">03</span><span class="f-title">Reels</span><span class="f-tag">VERTICAL VIDEO</span>
          <span class="f-chev"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"/></svg></span>
        </button>
        <div class="feat-body" id="fb3" role="region" aria-labelledby="fh3"><div class="fb-in"><div>
          <p>Indexed videos get a dedicated, full-height scroll-snap Reels view with keyboard and scroll navigation, details, likes and seeking. Local MP4, MOV, M4V, WebM and MKV are supported; playback uses the original where possible or streams converted segments on demand.</p>
          <p class="f-mono2">↑ ↓ to move between reels · ← → also work</p>
        </div></div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="feat rv" style="--d:.15s">
        <button class="feat-head" id="fh4" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="fb4">
          <span class="f-no">04</span><span class="f-title">Profiles per folder</span><span class="f-tag">IDENTITY</span>
          <span class="f-chev"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"/></svg></span>
        </button>
        <div class="feat-body" id="fb4" role="region" aria-labelledby="fh4"><div class="fb-in"><div>
          <p>Each indexed folder containing media, including nested folders, gets its own App Folder page: editable name and description, cover image, post counts, a grid, and a Reels tab when videos exist. Highlight circles come from child directories inside its reserved <code>stories/</code> folder.</p>
          <p class="f-mono2">Example profile: AnimalPlanet/ · 76 posts · 5 reels</p>
        </div></div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="feat rv" style="--d:.2s">
        <button class="feat-head" id="fh5" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="fb5">
          <span class="f-no">05</span><span class="f-title">Places</span><span class="f-tag">EXIF GPS</span>
          <span class="f-chev"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"/></svg></span>
        </button>
        <div class="feat-body" id="fb5" role="region" aria-labelledby="fh5"><div class="fb-in"><div>
          <p>After you prepare the optional GeoNames dataset in Settings, GPS-tagged photos can be grouped by nearby city and explored through Places. Coordinates come from EXIF; place names come from a downloaded local dataset. Matching runs offline, with approximate matches labeled.</p>
          <p class="f-mono2">GPS EXIF + optional local GeoNames dataset → nearby city</p>
        </div></div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="feat rv" style="--d:.25s">
        <button class="feat-head" id="fh6" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="fb6">
          <span class="f-no">06</span><span class="f-title">Likes &amp; Saved</span><span class="f-tag">LOCAL STATE</span>
          <span class="f-chev"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"/></svg></span>
        </button>
        <div class="feat-body" id="fb6" role="region" aria-labelledby="fh6"><div class="fb-in"><div>
          <p>Heart a post or save it into a collection. Signed-in admin and viewer sessions share likes and saved collections stored in local SQLite. In public mode, favorites and collections stay in that browser instead. Nothing is synced to a social engagement service.</p>
          <p class="f-mono2">SQLite for signed-in sessions · localStorage in public mode</p>
        </div></div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="feat rv" style="--d:.3s">
        <button class="feat-head" id="fh7" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="fb7">
          <span class="f-no">07</span><span class="f-title">Search &amp; Library</span><span class="f-tag">INDEX</span>
          <span class="f-chev"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"/></svg></span>
        </button>
        <div class="feat-body" id="fb7" role="region" aria-labelledby="fh7"><div class="fb-in"><div>
          <p>Explore offers a discovery grid and searches indexed folders by name and path. Library lets you search and sort all indexed folders; both load results incrementally. Foldergram reads its SQLite index, with thumbnails and previews created during scanning or on demand, depending on your settings.</p>
          <p class="f-mono2">Explore · indexed folder search · paginated Library</p>
        </div></div></div>
      </div>
      <a class="feats-more rv" href="https://docs.foldergram.app/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
        full documentation · docs.foldergram.app
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M7 17 17 7M9 7h8v8"/></svg>
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
